<div class="acc__body" id="a6" hidden><div class="acc__content">
<p><strong>To receive transfers in U.S. dollars at FACEBANK.</strong><br>ABA 021502189 o SWIFT: FILCPR22<br>FACEBANK International<br>17 Road 2, Suite 600<br>Guaynabo, Puerto Rico 00968-1787</p>
<p><strong style="letter-spacing: 0.128px; background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)">Para recibir euros</strong></p>
<p>Beneficiary: BANK OF AMERICA</p>
<p>Swift: BOFAIE3X</p>
<p>IBAN: IE54BOFA99006155797018</p>
<p>Referencia 1: FACEBANK INTERNATIONAL – 52203-LA</p>
<p>Reference 2: FFC “Full name of the client and FACEBANK account number"</p>
<p><strong>Required:</strong> Fill in the reference field with the details of the client receiving the funds at FACEBANK.</p>
<p><strong>To receive transfers in other currencies.</strong></p>
<p>Communicate with <a href="mailto:servicios@facebank.pr">servicios@facebank.pr</a> to receive instructions for other currencies</p>
<p>IMPORTANT: FACEBANK actively combats wire transfer fraud. For this reason, we do not provide wire transfer confirmations. If you have been informed that you will receive a transfer from FACEBANK and require additional information, you must contact the originator directly. We cannot provide any information to non-clients. In addition to the commercially reasonable security measures defined under the provisions of the Uniform Commercial Code (UCC) Funds Transfer Act, FACEBANK implements a wide range of security measures to monitor and detect fraud. Any suspected fraud cases are reported to the authorities of the applicable jurisdiction, regulatory agencies, and INTERPOL. These reports include all available data, including information about the complainant</p>
